+# Quantizing SenseNova-Loop-9B to EXL3
+
+One EXL3 checkpoint that the CUDA `qwen3_5` engine (RTX 16 GB) and the Metal runner both
+read: one pack per recipe, Mac and RTX alike. SenseNova-Loop-9B is Qwen3.5-9B with a shared-weight loop over layers [4, 28) and manifold-constrained
+hyper-connection (mHC) streams; the EXL3 layout is [exllamav3](https://github.com/turboderp-org/exllamav3)'s
+own, so its tooling reads the pack unchanged.
+
+Credit: EXL3 is exllamav3's format, quantizer and calibration set (turboderp); its trellis codebooks are
+QTIP's (Tseng, Chee, Sun, Kuleshov, De Sa, [arXiv:2406.11235](https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.11235)).
+
+## The layout
+
+- Stock exllamav3 output under HF tensor names, with `mul1` everywhere. Every quantized linear is
+  `<prefix>.trellis` i16 `[K/16, N/16, 16*bits]`, `<prefix>.suh` f16 `[K]`, `<prefix>.svh` f16 `[N]` and a
+  zero-size `<prefix>.mul1` marker: `self_attn.{q,k,v,o}_proj`, `linear_attn.{in_proj_qkv,in_proj_z,out_proj}`,
+  `mlp.{gate,up,down}_proj` and `lm_head`.
+- `embed_tokens.weight` stays BF16 (`-eb 16`). The Mac reads it from the mapped file, so it costs no GPU
+  residency there.
+- Copied from the source, never quantized: every norm (zero-centred as HF ships it, no `w + 1`),
+  `linear_attn.{conv1d.weight, A_log, dt_bias, in_proj_a.weight, in_proj_b.weight}`, the mHC routers
+  (`mhc_attn.{weight,bias}`, `mhc_ffn.{weight,bias}`, f32) and `loop_gate.*`. `model.visual.*` and `mtp.*`
+  are not in the pack.
+- `config.json` keeps SenseNova's `model_type: sensenova_loop`, `architectures`, `loop_settings` and `mhc`,
+  with the converter's `quantization_config` merged in.
+
+The CUDA loader accepts both stored dtypes for the small tensors: f32 `A_log`, `dt_bias` and
+`linear_attn.norm`, bf16 `in_proj_a`/`in_proj_b`, and today's bf16/f16 forms for stock packs.
+
+## Quantize
+
+exllamav3 at `turboderp-org/exllamav3@8c593e4e5c88da76a4aaf8f1b1838bb7c1fce4e0` in its own venv, with
+`TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=12.1`. Source: `sensenova/SenseNova-Loop-9B@329a65f701ba8c48b73c30d0cbaa6f0449733673`
+(BF16), and `Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B` for the control. Run it niced (`nice -n 19 ionice -c3`) on a machine with one
+large GPU; the measured run used a DGX Spark.
+
+[`tools/exl3_sensenova_chain.sh`](../tools/exl3_sensenova_chain.sh) runs steps 1 to 4 for SenseNova, then for the
+stock control when `EXL3_STOCK` is set, plus the task-gate references (`tools/exl3_gate_ref.py`: BF16 greedy, 64
+tokens on a prose, a code and a reasoning prompt). It resumes after the last finished step, holds
+`EXL3_GPU_LOCK` for one GPU step at a time and refuses a step below 40 GiB of MemAvailable. The steps by hand (`$WORK` is any working directory):
+
+exllamav3 cannot trace SenseNova: `sensenova_loop` is not one of its architectures and its `qwen3_5` forward
+has no loop and no mHC, so a calibration forward there would feed every layer the wrong activations. Instead
+capture the Hessians from the real transformers model and hand them to exllamav3's converter, which trusts a
+tensor's `hin` instead of tracing it.
+
+### 1. Present the text tower to exllamav3
+
+```bash
+python3 tools/exl3_attach_sensenova.py shim --source $WORK/bf16 \
+  --out $WORK/shim
+python3 tools/exl3_attach_sensenova.py shim --source $WORK/stock-qwen35-9b-bf16 \
+  --out $WORK/shim-stock
+```
+
+The shim is a directory of symlinks: the source's shards, tokenizer and generation config, with the text tower's
+config at the root, `architectures` `["Qwen3_5ForCausalLM"]` and `model_type` `qwen3_5_text`. exllamav3's
+`Qwen3_5ForConditionalGeneration` config requires a `vision_config`; the CausalLM one reads the same
+`model.language_model.*` keys without it. Shards are shared, not rewritten; the mHC, vision and MTP tensors sit
+inside them and are never asked for. The stock control takes the same shim, so both packs have one layout.
+
+### 2. Hessians, once per model
+
+```bash
+python3 -I tools/exl3_hessians.py --source $WORK/bf16 --shim $WORK/shim \
+  --out $WORK/hess/sensenova --device cuda:0
+python3 -I tools/exl3_hessians.py --source $WORK/stock-qwen35-9b-bf16 \
+  --shim $WORK/shim-stock --out $WORK/hess/stock --device cuda:0
+```
+
+The script loads the BF16 model with transformers and `trust_remote_code`, takes exllamav3's default
+calibration rows (`cal_rows=250`, `cal_cols=2048`) through exllamav3's own tokenizer of the shim, and registers a
+forward pre-hook on every linear the layout quantizes. Each hook accumulates `H += xᵀx` in f32 over the
+batch's tokens, drops non-finite rows, and divides by the token count at the end.
+
+- **The loop needs no special case.** Layers [4, 28) execute twice and the hook fires on both visits, so
+  their Hessian is the sum over both input distributions, which is the objective for one shared weight.
+- **mHC needs none either.** The hooks see the branch output each linear really receives (pre-weighted
+  stream mix, then norm); the routers stay f32 and are not quantized.
+- Linears that share an input share one accumulator and one file per key: q/k/v, `in_proj_qkv`/`z`,
+  `mlp.gate`/`up`. `o_proj`, `out_proj` and `down_proj` have their own.
+- `lm_head`'s input is the final norm's output, captured through a hook on the backbone's norm, so the
+  forward never builds the `[rows, vocab]` logits.
+- Memory is about 20 GB of f32 Hessians, dominated by `down_proj` at K=12288 (302 MB packed, x32).
+
+Each file is `{out}/{key}.safetensors` with `hin`, f32, as the packed upper triangle
+(`n(n+1)/2` values), the shape `--hessians` reads. `--plan-only` prints the keys and their captures without
+loading a model.
+
+### 3. Convert, one run per recipe
+
+```bash
+python convert.py -i $WORK/shim -o $WORK/exl3/sn-5.0 \
+  -w $WORK/work-sn-5.0 -b 5.0 -hb 6 -eb 16 -cb mul1 \
+  --hessians $WORK/hess/sensenova --out_scales always -d 0 --no_swap
+```
+
+The recipe files in [`exl3-recipes/`](exl3-recipes/) map to the flags: `bits` to `-b`, `head_bits` to `-hb`,
+`embed_bits` to `-eb`, `codebook` to `-cb`, `out_scales` to `--out_scales`. The same Hessians serve every
+width, so one capture pass feeds all three runs. `--out_scales always` because `auto` decides gate/up from
+calibration statistics a Hessian-only run does not collect.
+
+Watch the log for `No precomputed Hessian for <key>`: every quantized key must have a file, or the tensor is
+quantized uncalibrated. Repeat for `4.0` and `6.0`, then for the stock control at all three, each into its own
+output directory.
+
+### 4. Attach the extras and report
+
+```bash
+python3 tools/exl3_attach_sensenova.py attach --source $WORK/bf16 \
+  --converted $WORK/exl3/sn-5.0 --recipe sn-5.0
+```
+
+This copies the mHC and `loop_gate` tensors into `model-sensenova-extras.safetensors`, adds them to
+`model.safetensors.index.json`, restores SenseNova's `config.json` with the converter's
+`quantization_config` (plus the recipe name and calibration shape), copies the tokenizer and chat template,
+and prints every shard's size and sha256 for the hand-off. Without the extras (the stock control) it still
+restores the config and prints the report.
+
+## Gates
+
+The Mac tier's footprint gate and teacher-forced top-1 numbers are in the Metal plan; the RTX cells
+(`6.0`/`5.0`/`4.0`, bf16 and fp8 KV at 8k/32k/128k under `TENSORFOLD_CUDA_MEMORY_LIMIT_GB=15.0`) and the
+quality gates are in the EXL3 spec. The stock Qwen3.5-9B at the same recipe is the control: SenseNova's loss
+against BF16 must be no worse than the control's plus noise.
